summary: Test for VM-related kernel tunables validate.
description: |
    Test for VM-related kernel tunables validate.

    The test works as follows:
        checking if the tunable value correct one by one.

    See
    https://issues.redhat.com/browse/RHELMISC-3343
    https://issues.redhat.com/browse/VROOM-18563

    Test inputs:
        expected_values  <== An array of tunables and the expected values.
        current_value=$(cat "/proc/sys/vm/$tunable" 2>/dev/null)
        "$current_value" -eq "$expected_value"
    Expected results:
        [   PASS   ] :: $tunable expected: $expected_value, matches expected value!
    Results location:
        output.txt
contact: <pablmart@redhat.com>
id: a8f0d089-e595-4cff-9341-f5c7473d1686 
test: bash ./runtest.sh
framework: beakerlib
duration: 10m
